  "experiment": {
    "claim": "One of four variants of #169's initial-condition screen at 125 C / 50 mA, which re-tests #81 item 2 (a reported second, stable, non-regulating equilibrium: tt -> VOUT 2.093 V, FB 1.114 V, N_FBB 1.048 V; ss -> 2.014 V; fs -> 2.199 V) after #164 showed the method it rested on -- a `tran ... uic` with only v(vout) constrained -- is unreliable at the far gentler 27 C / 1 mA corner. The four variants run ONE circuit (sim/dropout-vs-load's DUT, C_OUT and ideal 50 mA load, VIN held at the corner supply) and vary ONLY the initial condition: V = #81's own contract (`.ic v(vout)=1.8` only, `uic`); F = the same `uic` analysis with all eleven nodes #169 names seeded at their intended-branch values; B = #164's variant-B contract (the same full `.ic`, no `uic`: constrained `.op`, then released); C = cold start from all-zero with the EN edge and the load ramped on once the loop is up. If F/B/C all settle inside the regulating window with a realizable node set while V does not, item 2 is a method artifact; if F/B/C also settle at #81's ~2.0-2.2 V state with all four realizability slacks >= 0, item 2 is a real second equilibrium. THIS VARIANT (H) is the historical control: variant V's testbench and analysis exactly (#81's contract: `.ic v(vout)=1.8` only, `tran ... uic`), but instantiating a FROZEN copy of design/ldo_3v3in_1v8out.sch at commit 64c17cb -- #81's own merge, before #90's thermal-shutdown re-size and #116's pass-device re-size -- held at #81's own VIN (3.60 V). It answers whether #81's circuit under #81's method ever reached the state #81 recorded, so a negative result on the current circuit (V/F/B/C) cannot be attributed to #90 or #116. It additionally dumps TS_SNS and TS_REF, and EA_OUT/TS_SNS/TS_REF/VOUT at #81's own 800 us time point, so #81's reported numbers can be matched node-by-node against this record. SUBSTANTIATES NO SPEC ROW: this is diagnostic evidence for design/README.md's \"#169\" section, kept in its own experiment slug for the same reason #164's screen was (sim/mc-ic-screen-a/-b/-d): measurements/build_characterization_report.py resolves a spec row's evidence from the lexicographically last record under the slug EVIDENCE_MAP maps it to, nothing maps to this slug, and a screen record must never be picked up as sim/dropout-vs-load's Dropout-row evidence. The vout_ss window is the ratified Output row's verbatim only so that 'regulating' has one fixed meaning across the four variants.",
